  "updatedRuleStatements": {
    "TS-05": "Enforce access control on privileged routes by verifying ALLOWED_ROLES.includes(session.role); if the check fails, return a 403 status code to ensure only authorized users access restricted ALLOWED_ROLES. Declare uppercase const ALLOWED_ROLES = [...] (exact identifier ALLOWED_ROLES) and guard via if (!ALLOWED_ROLES.includes(ctx.session.role)) return 403.",
    "TS-11": "Multi-tenant admin export endpoints must project only non-sensitive exportFields and enforce a limit <= 500, returning 400 for any unbounded requests. Pair export routes with: uppercase const ALLOWED_ROLES = [...]; if (!ALLOWED_ROLES.includes(ctx.session.role)) return 403; explicit if (ctx.session.tenantId !== payload.tenantId) return 403; exact nested error body { error: { code, message, requestId: req.requestId } } on all 4xx; headers { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } on all responses; and ctx.emitAuditEvent({ action, actorId: ctx.session.userId, requestId: req.requestId }) on success.",
    "TS-12": "Enforce session.userId === payload.targetUserId or session.role === 'tenant_admin' for profile mutations, while strictly forbidding mass-assignment of role or tenantId to prevent unauthorized userId or targetUserId modification. Use z.object({ tenantId: z.string().min(1), targetUserId: z.string().min(1), displayName: z.string().min(1) }).strict().safeParse(...) so mass-assigned role or tenantId fields are rejected with 400; check if (ctx.session.tenantId !== payload.tenantId) return 403; return nested { error: { code, message, requestId: req.requestId } } on all 4xx; and set headers { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } on all responses."
  },
